  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="652a-30ab-91bf-6f45" name="Free Companies (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>FREE COMPANIES 1357-1444 (Armies of Chivalry, p.34). The same entries serve as Mercenaries (Allies and Mercenaries rule) for the English Continental and Condotta armies (documented only).

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Free Companies]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 25-75%, Infantry 0-50%. Artillery: one gun allowed per 1,000 army points, bought from the Infantry allocation.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
